@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Library Policy";
}

<section class="policy-page">
    <header class="policy-heading">
        <span class="policy-eyebrow">PRIVATE LIBRARY</span>
        <h1>Library Policy</h1>
        <p>Our community is built on respect, safety, and a shared love of reading.</p>
    </header>

    <article class="policy-card">
        <section class="policy-section">
            <h2>Respectful Communication</h2>
            <p>All users are expected to communicate respectfully with other readers, event organizers, librarians, and administrators. The use of obscene, vulgar, abusive, discriminatory, or threatening language is not permitted.</p>
            <p>Harassment, bullying, intimidation, hate speech, personal attacks, insults, or any behavior intended to humiliate or offend another user are prohibited.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
            <h2>Responsible Use of the Library</h2>
            <p>Users must not publish offensive, unlawful, misleading, or inappropriate content in book reviews, ratings, event announcements, comments, or any other area of the website. Spam, advertising without permission, impersonation, and attempts to disrupt the service are also prohibited.</p>
            <p>Please respect other users' privacy. Do not publish another person's personal or contact information without their permission.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
            <h2>Moderation and Account Restrictions</h2>
            <p>Private Library may review, hide, or remove content that violates this policy. Depending on the seriousness or repetition of the violation, we may issue a warning, restrict access to certain features, temporarily suspend, or permanently block the account.</p>
            <p>These measures may be applied regardless of whether the account has an active paid subscription. Having a subscription does not exempt a user from the Library Policy or guarantee continued access when serious or repeated misconduct occurs.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
            <h2>Appealing an Account Restriction</h2>
            <p>If you believe that your account was restricted or blocked by mistake, you may contact the Private Library team and request a review. Please include your account username, the email address associated with the account, and a brief explanation of the situation. We will review the appeal and contact you using the details provided.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-contact">
            <h2>Contact Information</h2>
            <p>For questions about this policy, reports of inappropriate behavior, or appeals of account restrictions, contact us:</p>
            <a href="mailto:PrivatLibrary@gmail.com">PrivatLibrary@gmail.com</a>
        </section>
    </article>
</section>
